md-openmm build-top
====================================================================

Command
-------
  input                       parameter/FOL.sdf
  config                      build-top.config
  system out                  built.xml
  topology out                built.pdb

Resolved configuration
----------------------
  solute.kind                 ligand   (set)
  solute.peptide              None   (default)
  solute.ligand_forcefield    sage-2.2.1   (default)
  solute.ligand_charge_method am1bcc   (default)
  solute.compound_id          None   (default)
  solute.aliases              []   (default)
  solute.parameters           ./parameter   (set)
  solute.residue_name         None   (default)
  forcefield.protein          ff14SB   (default)
  solvent.model               TIP3P   (default)
  solvent.padding_nm          1.5   (default)
  solvent.box_shape           dodecahedron   (default)
  solvent.ionic_strength_molar0.15   (default)
  solvent.positive_ion        Na+   (default)
  solvent.negative_ion        Cl-   (default)
  solvent.cutoff_nm           1.0   (default)
  constraints.type            HBonds   (default)
  constraints.rigid_water     True   (default)

Input interpretation
--------------------
  interpreted as              single-molecule SDF
  coordinates                 supplied by the SDF, used as given (no embedding, no minimisation)
  residue name                FOL   (assigned deterministically)
  small-molecule FF           sage-2.2.1
  solvent treatment           explicit TIP3P, periodic
  protein FF                  not used
  water FF                    amber14/tip3p.xml

Preparation
-----------
  ligand       : [H]OC(=O)C([H])([H])C([H])([H])[C@@]([H])(C(=O)O[H])N([H])C(
  parameters   : LOCAL-OVBPIULPVIDEAO/param_a76881c75970 (reused (stated reference))
  protonation  : pH 7.0, 19 -> 19 hydrogens
  solvation    : 837 waters, ions {'NA': 2, 'CL': 2}, box dodecahedron (28.3 nm^3)
  box geometry : requested 1.5 nm padding -> solute-to-copy clearance 1.5 nm, reduced-box height 2.42007 nm (needs 2.1 nm for a 1.0 nm cutoff)
  system       : PME, cutoff 1.0 nm, switching False, dispersion correction True, Ewald tolerance 0.0005, HBonds

Validation
----------
  particle agreement          2566 atoms == 2566 particles  OK
  solute residue              FOL  OK
  periodicity                 periodic  OK (explicit)
  box vectors (nm)            (3.423 0.000 0.000); (0.000 3.423 0.000); (-1.711 -1.711 2.420)
  HMR                         NOT applied; masses are the force field's own, recommend 2.0 fs
  distinct H masses           [1.0079]

Counts
------
  atoms                       2566
  residues                    842
  solute atoms                51
  waters                      837
  ions                        {'NA': 2, 'CL': 2}
  forcefield                  openff-2.2.1

Outputs
